{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>A man of Elohim</b> — to tell that his blessing is fulfilled, for he was a man of Elohim and the prayer of the upright is His desire. Now Scripture calls Moses our master <b>a man of Elohim</b>, and likewise the other prophets, and Elijah, and others, and Scripture does not say <b>a man of YHWH</b>, but rather it says Moses the servant of YHWH (Deuteronomy 34:5), and the reason is known to every discerning person. And likewise by way of truth, this is the blessing, for it was from HaShem (Psalms 118:23), and likewise concerning Jacob it is said (Genesis 49:28), and this is what he spoke to them, their father. This blessing is what David said (Psalms 119:56), this was mine, for I have kept Your precepts — he hints to Zion, city of David, for there HaShem ordained the blessing, life forever, and the discerning will understand. And to this secret our Rabbis alluded in the Midrash when they said (Genesis Rabbah 100:12), 'And this is what their father spoke to them — a man is destined to arise like me to bless you, and from the place where I stopped, from there he begins.' Since Moses our master arose and opened for them with 'and this is the blessing,' from that very place where their father stopped for them — thus, 'and this is what their father spoke to them.' He said to them: these blessings, when do they reach you? From the hour that you receive the Torah, concerning which it is written, 'and this is the Torah, etc.' — for this word 'this' hints to the blessing, which is the Torah and which is the covenant, as it is written (Genesis 17:10), 'this is My covenant.' And I have already mentioned this (Leviticus 16:3)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {0 "The citation from Psalms 119:56 reads 'זֹאת הָיְתָה לִּי' in the Hebrew text with a dagesh-like doubling in the lamed; translated hyper-literally as written, though the standard form is without doubling."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:58:46.339305459Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}